!! Vitals

No count rests here: a number in a handoff goes stale the moment a hand commits. Each line names the
instrument that reads the tree; run it fresh before trusting any reading.

* ''Branch'' `feature/lararium-node-5`, ahead of `origin` — `git rev-list --count origin/feature/lararium-node-5..HEAD` reads the unpushed commits; the operator pushes. Unstaged in the tree and NOT a lane's to move: `.worktrees/`, `.claude/worktrees/`, and the `mempalace` submodule pointer — never commit, stash, or revert those. The `VSCode-TW5-Syntax` pointer reads differently: the operator PINNED it at `4afa852`, the released 3.0.0, and the grammar's own head stands ahead of that pin. A lane still leaves it alone; the operator moves it, and a `git log` on that gitlink shows their pin rather than drift.
* ''Unit suites'': each package's own, under a scratch `LAR_ROOT` with `LAR_BAGS` unset; `node --test tools/*.test.mjs` for the tools. An import failure reads as zero tests, so read the file count beside the test count.
* ''Typecheck'': `tools/typecheck-witness.sh`.
* ''Witness fleet'': `bash tools/witness-all.sh`, one at a time. It holds out `tree-clean`, `civic`, `crossing`, `herm-mesh` and `browser-weld`, which run by hand; `git status --porcelain` reads identical before and after a sound run.
* ''E2E'': every set rides the CI shards (`tools/e2e-shards.mjs`, `.github/workflows/e2e-shards.yml`; `E2E_SETS` names the sets and the merge gate checks each set's union). A local run of one file proves that file alone.
* ''CI'' (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): the operator pushes; `gh run list --branch feature/lararium-node-5` names the run for the pushed head, and anything committed after it waits for the next push. `held-out.yml` runs weekly or by hand; no hosted run of it has yet read green.
* ''The docker mesh'' (by hand): `crossing-witness`; `node tools/mesh-pins.mjs --up` stands the mesh pinned; `herm-mesh-witness` carries `node/alpha` across three hops; `mesh-scenarios nexus`. A hearth whose log carries a `[lararium] fatal:` line reads as not stood.
* ''HEADS-UP — the operator's live `~/.lares` vessel'' holds an earlier shape: clocked device edges, unsigned rolls, pin sidecars carrying `expiry`, undotted circle stamps, and a lineage-less charter. None verifies on this build. Do NOT stand that vessel here; it needs a fresh start, by hand (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/fresh-start`).
* ''Known environmental reds'': `lararium-tw5` `tests/syncer-back-parity.e2e.test.ts` (Chromium legs) and `tests/meme-routes.e2e.test.ts` fail when a browser or server socket stands absent; the browser suite reads `no tests` under a `HOME` that holds no Playwright Chromium.

