<<~ ahu #/cold-start>>

!! Cold start

# `export LAR_ROOT=/tmp/lar-scratch-<you>` before any in-tree boot or store-touching `lares` command — `LAR_ROOT` moves the store, the bags root and every projection mirror root; `LAR_BAGS` alone moves only the bags root, and the projection still writes the tracked `bags/` and `wikis/`. A bare in-tree boot writes into the tracked tree, and `tools/tree-clean-witness.sh` reads that as red. The staged e2e set takes a scratch `LAR_ROOT` per vessel and NO global `LAR_BAGS`. A single `lares meme normalize|check` reads files and needs only a scratch `LAR_BAGS`.
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, then `pnpm -r build`, then `pnpm --filter @lararium/tw5 build:tw5-vendor` (the TW5 core blob `head-parity` and `scripts/smoke-plugin-boot.ts` need — `pnpm -r build` does not produce it), then `node tools/stamp-build.mjs`.
# A fresh `git worktree` holds empty submodules (`TiddlyWiki5`, `VSCode-TW5-Syntax`, `mempalace`); populate them before building there.
# ''A founding wants a human route on a TTY.'' With no TTY it refuses `CredentialTtyRefusal`, and no flag or environment variable carries a credential. A harness founds through the test door: `tools/test-scratch-marker.mjs` stages the root, `tools/seed-test-custody.mjs` names the published test route, then `lares vessel found --skip-build`. The door acts only on a root the stager marked.
# ''The container'': `tools/lares-container.sh` (`up`, `down`, `found`, `logs`; any other argv runs the CLI inside the standing container) over `docker-compose.surface.yml`. ''The browser surface'': `tools/browser-ci.sh` over `docker-compose.browser-ci.yml`, one project and image tag per builder (`BROWSER_CI_PROJECT`, `BROWSER_CI_IMAGE`).
# `lares-cli` `tests/pour-repave.test.ts` needs the dev-root marker (`LAR_DEV_REPO_ROOT=1` or the gitignored `lar-dev-root.json`).
# The tw5 plugin bundle (`packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/lares-memetic-wikitext.json`, `plugins/standalone/*`, `src/plugin-tiddler.generated.ts`) rides in git and must equal a fresh build — rebuild after any tw5 source or tiddler change and commit it with the change. CI's `build-freshness` job checks it.
# A `browser-weld` run in any tree owes that tree a `pnpm --filter @lararium/web build` afterwards (see #/wounds, the Pronaos receipt).
# Run `bash tools/witness-all.sh` for the whole fleet — a hand-picked subset of witnesses reads greener than the tree.
# Read `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot` (the boot seed), then this carrier, then `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road`, then the rulings memory (`project_grammar_as_tiddlers_rulings.md`) before touching grammar, frame, or ingest code.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/wounds>>

!! Open wounds, ranked

Each wound names the path of `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-road` that closes it.
The rulings owed read in ''Pending operator rulings''.

''HIGH''
# ''Custody rests bare outside the tree and the root'' (SUBSTRATE, the seal). The slot tree and the custody root seal from birth; every other `hot` and `cold` carrier still rests as its own writer leaves it, and the keyhive archive rests cleartext in the state home where no archive passphrase stands. No boot path opens the VK. `lares vault unbind --rotate` refuses `RotationPreflightRefusal` on every real founded vessel, since `vessel-next` rests bare from birth.
# ''The main tree's workspace links read ABSOLUTE'' (environment; the controller's or the operator's hand). The links under `packages/*/node_modules/@lararium/` point at absolute host paths, so they dangle inside any repo-mounted container: `civic`, `crossing` and `herm-mesh` read red in the main tree and green in a worktree whose links pnpm wrote relative. Cure: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`; where the links stay absolute, remove those `@lararium` link directories first and install again. The engine fold's proofs want this cured, or a worktree with its own install.
# ''No browser has yet joined a node live'' (the shore). The device admit, the face join, the granted recipe and a typed edit read back from the node all stay unproven; whether the wiki worker still faults on a save or a popup stands unmeasured in this tree. The node owes the durability receipt.

''MEDIUM''
# ''The steward signer'' (KAHU PLANE). The docker `meme` scenario fails at "B edits, promotes": the steward gets named by a per-Nexus LEAF key, while the realm-bag co-sign looks for the persona ROOT key. The signer stands RULED (the worn face or a quorum Handle, never the root); the build owes it, and neither a root workaround nor a leaf fallback closes it.
# ''A faceless vessel half-lands `act CREATE`'' (GROUND). In the container the verb answers a veil error advising a re-found, yet the bag registers; on the host it reads `outcome-unknown` and an `ingest --apply` behind it reads `cap-denied`. The floor should refuse content verbs by name before any registration.
# ''A re-scan after `ingest --apply` reads the carrier `new`'' (GROUND). `recordLandedPacks` (`packages/lares-cli/src/ingest-core.ts`) records an observation only for a result naming a `pack`; a single-meme carrier names none. Content stays safe (a second apply reads `noop`), but the watcher re-submits every wave and can never see a deletion.
# ''Recipe wiring lacks a vessel-level proof.'' No test drives a recipe that names an offering through a vessel path; the resolver tests prove the selector, never the wiring on the node daemon VM, the browser pool or the browser daemon VM.
# ''Refold answers may overclaim.'' `represented:true` survives a re-presentation that found no dial, and `after-roll-awaited.test.ts` reads source shape only.
# ''A vite dev server's close rewrites the Pronaos receipt'' (the shore). `emitPronaosArtifactRecord().closeBundle` in `packages/lararium-web/vite.config.ts` runs on any close and writes whatever it holds, so a `browser-weld` run leaves three tools tests red until a web rebuild. Cure: both plugins take `apply: "build"`.
# ''`vessel stand --install` reaches outside `LAR_ROOT` before the founding can refuse'' (GROUND): `standup.ts` links into `~/.local/bin` and runs the mempalace install first, where `stand.ts` says founding stands the vessel and nothing else.

''LOW, by path''
# ''GROUND — retired bags.'' The write gate enumerates its verbs by hand (`action-handler.ts`); the refusal's `error.code` reads generic where its message names `bag-retired`; CLEAR on a retired bag still writes into the retired doc; a fresh CREATE of an empty bag stamps `count: 1`; the ingest preview ignores retirement; a wiki-island save and the watcher's ingest-back into a retired bag stand unprobed; canon still says DROP "marks the bag retired" (`action-handler.mem`) without the refusal that follows.
# ''GROUND — the quiet doors.'' REPACK's refusal sites sit outside the one hint helper and its synchronous refusal drops the request id (`act.ts`); the accepts walk misses computed flag reads (`stand.ts`, `meme.ts`); `main.ts` accepts an unread `--debug`; `stand.ts` documents `--init` and `--install` as synonyms where the vessel door rules no aliases; store refusals reach JSON under a generic code; `device-admit` carries `syncUrl: null` where `LAR_PUBLIC_URL` stands.
# ''GROUND — evergreen.'' Stale or archaeological prose in source: `open-node-vessel.ts` and `node-cas.ts` ("read fresh … never cached" over a captured boot epoch); `action-handler.ts` (LOAD "not implemented"); `persona-admit-flow.ts` (an offer may have "expired"); `cabal-vouch.ts` ("an expiry already past"); `lares.ts` (reboot-to-switch, `--expires`); `custody-prompt.ts` (the test door "refuses a root outside scratch"); `realm-plane.ts` (advises a `nexus refresh` no door answers); lane labels in test titles. Back-compat wording or tolerant readers: `index.ts` (node), `open-browser-vessel.ts`, `residency-actions.ts`, `daemon-vm-core.ts`, `nexus-publish.ts`, `ingest-core.ts`, `device-delegation.ts`, `lar-uris.ts`, `seal-reserve.ts`, `mesh-palace.ts` (a carried `expiry` field), `cleanup-days.ts`, `nexus-seal-seed.ts`, `archive-envelope.ts`.
# ''GROUND — custody's edges.'' The floor guard reads a carrier cut inside its 13-byte magic as `bare`; a short seat can write a charter that boots torn (`nexus-seal.ts`); a floor-class carrier standing alone founds; `setFoundingRoute` stands as a test seam in source; the custody wait can refuse falsely where no holder answers; `readTty` drops a pasted second line; `NameTooLong` did not fire on a root 150 bytes deep.
# ''SUBSTRATE — the seal's own.'' `vault status` gives three readings of one file (`key-class.ts` folds a policy and a byte fact into one `atRest` column); `assertNoOldShape` (`found.ts`) drives the sealed writer's check through a fake io whose writes throw — mesh should export the check; the unbind and the rotation run as two acts.
# ''The roll and the refold.'' An unbounded `afterRollChain` stage can stall later rolls and leave refold answers pending; `pokeSealHomeRefold` maps a failed refold to `none`; `tw5BinPath` records a constant rather than a measured path.
# ''The shore.'' The web defaults name port 8080 and the mode row never moves; the shared holder caches a refused lock for the worker's whole life.

''Aftermath owed'' (docs; no code)
* The CHANGELOG carries nothing past `NO GLOBAL NOW`: the retired-bag refusal, the custody door, the one claim, the parser and its accepts table, split-root ingest, the image and its shims, the every-set shards, the test door's marker law and the browser surface all wait for their block.
* Canon to re-true: `action-handler.mem` on DROP; a carrier for the container boundary; wherever the test door's "scratch" still reads as a temp-dir test; the browser surface's secure-context law beside `docker-compose.mesh.yml`'s.
* One sentence for the `CLAUDE.md` adapter note, the operator's to place: the CLI's ingest, watch and REPACK derive against `LAR_BAGS` and `LAR_WIKIS`, so "read neither" holds for the daemon's projection mirrors alone.

''Carried, unranked''
* Road (iv): surface-for-review.
* Q6: loans keyed by CID.
* A design call on `/cas` timing; whether the parallel-draft alert persists.
* `packages/lararium-sensorium/requirements.txt` calls the tree-sitter versions one (Python binding 0.26, CLI 0.27; both ABI 15).

''Pending operator rulings''
* ''The road's open questions'' — `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/open`: the seal-roll successor's name; a root-holding browser leaf's backup slot; the seat's cold next key at founding; a sealed receipt manifest for carriage; carriage across leaves.
* ''The two-voice herm'' (research done): may a herm speak in a voice of its own, or only through a share of one? `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/lamplighters#/open` strikes `operate ⊥ sign` and proposes a FROST Place-DID with the herm holding one share; its drift-ward splits the utterances — federation-facing and condemnation-relevant ones thresholded, local carry single-signed — and `#/immune`'s "herms present" (the victim testifies) reads beside "the least credible witness to its own neglect". The split stands as the ruling owed.
* ''The Lamplighters' question'': whether island-admin tending (`tend.repair`) reaches the herm's own `@daemon` signing key — ISOLATE it, or ACCEPT it and price the lost independent testimony (`lamplighters#/open`; its `role` line advertises it).
* ''Two Kairoses'': the fiction's KAIROS watches the noosphere across nodes and speaks unasked (`elyncia/Elyncia_02_The_Lares_DreamNet.md`); the code's Kairos names, as a pet-name, an unbuilt OAuth-refresh entity that waits for the right moment (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/reach-plane`). One entity, or two that share a name?
* ''The Codex crew's forks'', reconciled against the code in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/crew-handoff-codex#/reconciled`: the Offering Antigen scope (and the charter-inception identity it rests on); the crossing record's emission threshold and destination receipts; seam (b)'s altitude; `bag-residency.ts`'s home.

''Needs the operator''
* ''Grammar submissions'': whether the Nexus Kahu or the corpus-kahu receive them.
* ''The offering's `offer`/`witness` caps'' against the Lamplighter stack.
* ''Engine cadence, still open'' (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu` `#/contract`): who holds a cadence share; one daemon hosting two engine epochs; whether partial conformance lands before `kahuli engine` un-holds.
* ''Backstop seam (b), PHASE 5'' (`tests/meme-backstop.test.ts`): three child-edit shapes the test marks as the operator's call.
* ''Ruling-gated mesh modules'' (listed in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/index.ts`'s header): `recipe`, `readiness`, `reaction-graph` (canon memes pin their mesh `source-file`), `pronaos`, `offering-inspection` (own mesh-namespace memes). Each moves or stays only by ruling.
* ''The capture cell'' sits isolated for review in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-node/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/capture/`, `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/capture/`. Canon (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/capture-annotation-model`, the sensorium-machina S5 ruling) places capture in Python per stream with the TS @daemon coordinating only; the TS cell carries the live path. Rule: retire it to Python, or re-home it.

''Deferred by law or by the operator''
* ''Cloud carriers'' and the reading of "delegated keys" — until the operator can deploy to a cloud surface (`stable-founding-road#/the-road`).
* ''The Sensorium's logic'' (`packages/lararium-sensorium/**`, tw5 `form-layer/**`, mesh `ffz-project`, `clock-recovery`, coupling/metric modules): the measure-servo aliases in `ffz-project.ts`, one five-band ladder (Title case `ApertureBand`, the others derived), the `lar_feedback` output field name. It waits behind the working-Lararium milestone; frames inside it stay in scope for healing at any time.
* ''Tangle, the putback law, the tongue fold'' — gated on a real return trip and a whole regeneration of `packages/tree-sitter-memetic-wikitext` (mirror pairing, round-trip CI, Markdown injection into `hana`). The aka/weave rhyme (`memetic-wikitext-framing.mem` Annex) waits on tangle.
* ''A relay-stream profile'' — a stream of carriers belongs to the SYN-framed profile (`&#x0016;`, held in reserve); one `.mem` file frames one carrier. The profile defines batch framing and resynchronisation.
* ''A carrier seal'' — re-mint an attestation mark with a computed, verified check when signing lands.
* ''EOT targeting'' — what a resolved `-> to=` would name (the declared-unresolved meaning stands).
* ''A standing whole-tree gate'' (build every package from clean, run every witness and suite) — run as a spirit pass, not built into the CLI or a trigger.

