!! Map ahead

# Bring the pending rulings to the operator before any lane builds against one.
# ''Operator priority'': a working Lararium comes first — Live Wiki Browser -><- Live Node, under manual QA on one machine. The live test that follows runs with two operators on two machines, and the face-switch act, the cabal plane, the custody seal and the engine fold all land before it.
# Walk the road at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-road`: GROUND → SUBSTRATE (the engine fold, then the custody seal) → HARBOR → KAHU PLANE (realms and the steward signer, R-CHARTER, R-WIRE, then R-KAHU, the engine offers and R-EMBER) → ONE FACE → TWO HEARTHS, with the shore's rungs beside it. Every shape-changing slice lands before the second human contracts in.
# Close `#/wounds` beside the path each wound names; write the aftermath it owes.
# Exercise the quoteblock floor (both grains), the child gate and the persisted parallel drafts in the live wiki, against real concurrent browser saves, and turn every surprise into a test.
# Regenerate the tree-sitter grammar whole against the released TW5-Syntax 3.0.0 (the submodule pointer reads `4afa852`) — the regeneration unlocks tangle and the publication track.
# Publication: the `text/markdown; variant=memetic-markdown` registration, the provisional `lar` scheme (after `lar-uri` gains its Security section), the vnd./prs. media type, and `draft-fontany-*` / `draft-tiddlywiki-*` (the TW5 pairs move to kramdown-rfc2629 when the community walk begins). The standalone `$:/plugins/lares/memetic-wikitext` artifact ships from `packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/standalone/`.

